        <p>WARR IN GT 0 N "MUSICAL SOCIETY SECOND SUBSCRIPTION CONCERT. PARR HALL, MONDAY NEXT, DEC. 27Tli. HANDEL'S "MESSIAH." CHORUS AND ORCHESTRA OF OVER 200 PERFORMERS.. PLAN NOW OPEN at Mr. R. H. Pearson's Music Warehouse, Bridge st. For prices and other particulars see posters.</p>
        <p>QILN.RESPEARE THEATRE, LIVERPOOL. kJ Managing Director: Mn. WENTWORTH CROKE. MONDAY, DEC. 27th at 1.30 and 7. p.m. The Grand Christmas Pantomime "DICK WHIT I'INGTON AND HIS CAT." Miss CARRIE MOORE as "DICK." Mr. HARRY RANDALL as" THE COOK." Mr. TOM FOY as "IDLE JACK," supported by a Brilliant Company of equally well-known Artistes. Matinees at 2, Tuesday, Deoember 28th; Wednesday 29th, Thursday 30th; Saturday, January Ist, 1910 and every Monday, Wednesday and Saturday until further notice. Every evening at 7 o'clock. Box Office 10 to 4. daily. Telephones 1327 and 245 Royal.</p>
        <p>ROY EIL COURT THEATRE, WARRINGTON.</p>
