      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-12-24_WidnesExaminer_art0007" n="art0007">
        <head>COUNTY PALATINE OF CHESTER.</head>
        <p>COUNTY PALATINE OF CHESTER.</p>
        <p>NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN, that the next, GENERAL QUARTER SESSIONS of the Peace for the COUNTY PALATINE OF CHESTER will he holden at the CASTLE OF CHESTER, in and for the said County, on MONDAY, the 3rd day of JANUARY, 1910, at Half-past Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon when the Grand Jury will be empannelled. The hearing of all Appeals arising within the Petty Sesiional Divisions of Broxton. Chester Castle, Dares. bury, Addisbury, Nantwich, Runcorn. Winsford, and Wirral, forming the Chester District, and the trials of all prisoners committed from the last-mentioned Divisions, will take place at such Sessions. The arand and Petty Juries for the Chester District must be in attendance at the Castle of Chester, at the Opening of the Court on MONDAY, the 3rd day of January, 1910, at Half-past Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon. THE COURT will be Adjourned to the COURT HOUSE, KNUTSFORD, on WEDNESDAY, the sth DAY OF JANUARY, 1910, at Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon.</p>
        <p>- The hearing of all Appeals arising within the Petty Sessional Divisions of Altrincham, BuckloNv, Dukinfleld, Middlewich, Sandbacb, Congleton, Northwich, Prest- bury and Stockport, forming the Knutsford District, and the trials of all prisoners committed from such Divisions, will take place at such Adjourned Sessions. The Grand and Petty Juries for the Knutsford District must be in attendance at the Court House, Knutsford, at the Opening of the Court on WEDNESDAY, the sth day of January, 1910, at Eleven o'clock in the Fore- noon.</p>
        <p>REGINALD POTTS, Clerk of the Peace for the County of Chester. Chester, 20th December, 1909. IN PARLIAMENT. SESSION 1909. WARRINGTON CORPORATION BILL.</p>
        <p>MEE lING OF ELECTORS OF THE COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON TO BE HELD PURSUANT TO THE PROVISIONS OF THE BOROUGH FUNDS ACT, 1003.</p>
        <p>OTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that the Mayor, 11 Aldermen and Burgesses of the County Borough of Warrington have resolved in accordance with the provisions of the Borough Funds Act 1872 to promote a Bill in Parliament in the next Session intituled "A Bill to empower the Corporation of Warrington to construct Bridges; Street Improvements and other Works; to make further and better provisions with regard to the Gas and Electricity Undertakings of the Corporation ; and to improve the health and local government of the Borough and for other purposes." The objects of the Bill are To confer further powers on the Corporation of Warrington, with regard to the following matters :</p>
        <p>New Bridge to-replace present Warrington Bridge; Construction of New Bridge over River Mersey ; River Walls ; Widening and Improvement of Streets and Roads ; Purchase of Garven House Property; Purchase of Lands by Compulsion or Agreement; Extension of Town Hall, Public Baths and Technical School ; Sale of Howley Recreation Ground ; power to deal with proceeds of sale Further provisions as to the Gas, Water, and Electricity Undertakings of the Corporation ; Supply of Electricity in Bulk ; Motor Omnibuses; Licensini, of Drovers, &amp;c.; Registration of Dairies and Millhops ; Regulation of Fried Fish Dealers and Hairdressers and Barbers ; Ice Cream Pro- visions ; Common Lodging-houses; New Streets and Buildings ; Sewers and Drains ; Infectious Disease and Sanitary Provisions ; Subscriptions ; Borrowing Powers ; Rates ; Police Provisions; Incorporation, Amendment, and Repeal of Acts. The Bill also contains various clauses to carry out the purposes aforesaid which are naually inserted in Bills of like kind.</p>
        <p>The Bill was deposited in the House of Commons on the 17th instant.</p>
        <p>Copies of the Bill may be inspected and purchased (at the price of 2s. 6d. per copy) at the Office of the Town Clerk, Town Hall, Warrington, between the hours of 10 o'clock in the forenoon and 4 o'clock in the after- noon on every week day for 14 days after the 24th day of December instant and extracts may by taken there- from free of charge. AND NOTICE IS HEREBY FURTHER GIVEN that in accordance with the provisions of the Borough Funds Act 1903 a Public Meeting of the Electors for the time being enrolled in the register of Parochial Electors in force for the Township and Borough of Warrington will be held on FRIDAY the 21st day of JANUARY, 1910, at the Parr Hall, Warrington, at 7.30 o'clock in the evening for the purpose of consider- ing the promotion ofthe said Bill. At, the said public meeting of Electors a resolution will be submitted in favour of the promotion of the whole bill, or if the said meeting request that resolutions in favour of the promotion of any part or parts or clause or clauses of the said Bill be put separately, but together covering the promotion of the whole Bill, resolutions to give effect to that request will accordingly be submitted to such meeting. _</p>
        <p>DATED this Twenty-fourth day of December 1909. WM. J. FORSHAW, Mayor.</p>
      </div>
