      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-12-24_WidnesExaminer_art0099" n="art0099">
        <head>EMPIRE SKATING RINK.</head>
        <p>EMPIRE SKATING RINK.</p>
        <p>Hockey Matches.</p>
        <p>An exciting hockey match vvas witnessed on Tuesday night. when the 'Empire team met Ardwick Imperial. The Empire team turned out as follows :—Berry (goal), Hulme (back), Walton, Wadsworth and Readon (for- wards). The Empire team were the better five, and hard luck was their lot in not scoring more frequently. In the first half Wadsworth and Hulme were conspicuous, and a shot through Ardwick's goal was disallowed. At half-time there was no score. In the second half the locals again scored two goals, which were disallowed. Hulme, however, came to the rescue and scored a beautiful goal, after running round all the opposing team. Shortly afterwards Ritson, for Ardwick, captured the ball, and with a hard knock evaded the home custodian, and equalised. No other goals ensued and the game ended after a splendid struggle in a draw. The Empire team journeyed to Broughton on Wednesday night and were defeated by .1-1. The Empire team was as follows : Bowcock (goal), Hulme (back), Walton, Wadsworth and Readon (forwards.) The Broughton team were con- spicuous for superior skill and after a few minutes play Wilson scored a goal which was soon after followed with another. Wadsworth a few minutes before half time scored the visitors' only goal. Half-time arrived with the score at 2-1. In the second half two more goals were scored by Broughton and the game ended with the score: Broughton four goals, Empire one. The waltzing competition announced for last night has been postponed.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-12-24_WidnesExaminer_art0100" n="art0100">
        <head>CHRISTMAS WEEK.</head>
        <p>CHRISTMAS WEEK.</p>
        <p>"Directly we begin to live we begin to die" said Kirke one of our greatest physiologists. To prolong life is the desire of all. The surest and best way is to take</p>
        <p>HARRIS'S ANTI-DYSPEPTIC PILLS</p>
        <p>A sure and safe cure for all troubles of Stomach and Liver. They are a boon to oil who suffer from Dyspepsia in its many forms. Also for CONSTIPATION, BILIOUSNESS, SICKNESS, FLATULENCE. They will also immediately relieve PILES, FISTULA and GRAVEL.</p>
        <p>A Doctor says :—" I object to nostrums of all kinds, patent or otherwise, but have to acknowledge that your pills have much benetitted my wife, relieving her of many distressing symptoms and insomnia.." Testimony such as this from a medical man speaks for itself. Follow the example of the doctor's wife. Prove for yourself how good a remedy you have to hand at a small cost. NURSE HARRIS'S ANTI-DYSPEPTIC PILLS, GREASBY, BIRKENHEAD. Boxes, is. lid., is. 9d., 2s. 9d.</p>
        <p>A peep into the rink yesterday disclosed many decorators, busily engaged in decorating the rink with numerous lanterns in addition to those already there, of different shapes and sizes. Festoons of artificial flowers were also being placed from roof to side, which when the powerful flash lights which are being erected play upon them will produce beautiful kaleidoscopic) effects. In addition there are several special attrac- tions including the following: To-night, Mistletoe session which will undoubtedly prove very amusing; Boxing night, Great Bon-Bon night. On Thursday afternoon there will be a special session for the children, when Santa Claus and a Christmas Tree will be introduced. In the evening there will be a Two Step Competition and on New Year's Eve, special chime music will be played. During the coming week the rink will be open in the evening session until 10.30 instead of 10 o'clock. The floor has been re-surfaced and patrons pr onounce it perfect.</p>
      </div>
