      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-12-24_WidnesExaminer_art0156" n="art0156">
        <head>' KING AND QUEEN OF THE BELGIANS.</head>
        <p>' KING AND QUEEN OF THE BELGIANS.</p>
        <p>King Albert is the hope of the Belgian Monarchy. He is a mm of altogether different st imp from King Leopold, and he and his beautiful wife should restore to the Throne of Belgium much of that dignity which it lost during die reign of the la`ely deceased ruler. The new King is of a studious nature; he has travelled much in every country of Europe, and on his majority he made a long trip to the United States. His Consort shares the tastes and pursuits of her husband. She is a daughter of the late Duke Karl Theodor of Bavaria, and her marriage with tLe present King of the Belgians was in every way a love match.</p>
        <p>THE GRAND DUKE I MICHAEL.</p>
        <p>The late Grand Duke Michael Nicolaivitch, great-uncle of the Czar, was the last survivor of the chi!dren of Czar Nicholas I. He took part in the derence of Sebastopol, and won the St. George's Cross for gallan;ry at the battle of Inkerman. He was a General Field Marshal of the Russian Army, the highest distinction that can be canferred on a Russian soldier.</p>
        <p>The late Grand 'Duke was the father of the Grand Duke Michael of Keele Hall, Staffordshire.</p>
