      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-12-24_WidnesExaminer_art0157" n="art0157">
        <head>WHERE KING LEOPOLD</head>
        <p>WHERE KING LEOPOLD</p>
        <p>IS BURIED.,</p>
        <p>. Contrary to his expressed wish, the remains of the late King Leopold were accorded a State funeral. The Government, it is statei, took this step solely 0 C 3 npensate thc tradesmen of Brussels for the loss they will sustain during the coming Spring throu;h the Court being in mourning, and the consequent cancelling of social festivities. For the like reason, the new King consented to make a triumphal entry into the capital on horse-, back, in glittering military uniform, and attended by a numerous suite. Our illeitrAti94 ib9Wl glAlirch et St, Gudnle, i Brionls, where the dead Iciug lies buried.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-12-24_WidnesExaminer_art0158" n="art0158">
        <head>PRINCESS STEPHANIE.</head>
        <p>PRINCESS STEPHANIE.</p>
        <p>King Leopold died without being reconciled fo his second daughter, Princess Stephanie. She quarrelled with her father because on the death of her first husband, Crown Prince Rudolph of Austria, she married Count Lonyay who was not of royal rank. King Leopold refused tc receive her when she visited Brussels tp place a wreath ort her mother's grays.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-12-24_WidnesExaminer_art0159" n="art0159">
        <p>working on the candidates being run on strict party tickets. A Commission has been con- sidering this question, . but it has not yet reported. There have been other plans put forward to secure fair representatfon of all opinions and parties, but it may be said that at present the whole subject is in the discussion stage. The increase in the number of triangular contests will force this question forward, and, I expect that the near Reform Bill will propose something on the subject, not improbably some simple system of transferable vote by which if a voter's first preference does not win, his second preference may gain his vote.</p>
        <p>:11</p>
      </div>
