        <p>APPROVED BY DOCTORS ! ! Durham Villa, Park-road, Hythe, Kent, June 12th, 1908.</p>
        <p>Dear Sir,—For the past years I have been troubled with Gout in my right big toe joint, and suffered great pain until I was told of your Gout Pills by a friend of mine, and determined to try them. But I cannot allow this opportunity to pass without writing you to express my admiration at their quick and efficient treatment, and I SHALL NEVER BE WITHOUT THENT._</p>
        <p>lam a dispenser of 31 years' standing, and in all my dispensing these many years I huvefailed to find anything do me good so quickly. The senior partner of my firm of doctors, I may say, approves of them. You are at liberty (fully) to make any use you like of this letter. Yours faithfully, EDWARD D. CULL, Dispenser. EADE'S GOUT PILLS Are perfectly safe in their action, eliminate all injurious matter, and are highly restorative. Sold everywhere in bottle Is. lid. and 2s. 9d. or sent post free for stamps or P.O.by the proprietor. GEORGE EADE, 232, Goswell road London'</p>
