      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-12-24_WidnesExaminer_art0186" n="art0186">
        <head>Exarc</head>
        <p>The Exarc</p>
        <p>DEATH OF COUNCILLOR SINGLETON.</p>
        <p>Many of our readers will deeply regret to hear of the death of Councillor Henry Singleton who passed away at his residence, 15, Bold-street at a quarter to five on Sunday evening. For some months the deceased gentleman, who would have been 43 years of age on Monday, had suffered from heart trouble but he attended to his public work until comparatively recently. Mr. Singleton was a native of Liverpool and in his early years was in business as a butcher in Liverpool, manaking his -mother's establishment. Returning to Widnes he carried on business there and was also prominently identified with municipal life,</p>
